1
00:00:09,920 --> 00:00:11,037
The End Morning, Miss Claire.

2
00:00:11,120 --> 00:00:12,473
Ready to start the day?

3
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:18,997
Oh, whoops, I'm sorry about that.

4
00:00:19,080 --> 00:00:20,551
I didn't hurt you, did I?

5
00:00:21,480 --> 00:00:23,417
No, but do try to be a bit more careful.

6
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:25,441
Honestly, Lene, you should know -

7
00:00:32,440 --> 00:00:34,616
It's been a while since we lost Lene,

8
00:00:34,720 --> 00:00:37,937
but Miss Claire's still having
a really hard time moving on.

9
00:00:38,020 --> 00:00:40,255
I wish there was something I could do.

10
00:00:40,340 --> 00:00:41,170
I know!

11
00:00:41,260 --> 00:00:44,357
How about I whip up something
sugary and delicious for you?

12
00:00:44,440 --> 00:00:46,077
Where did this idea come from?

13
00:00:46,160 --> 00:00:47,760
Maybe fondant au chocolat?

14
00:00:47,880 --> 00:00:49,780
Or a decadent creme brulee?

15
00:00:50,060 --> 00:00:53,178
Heck, why pick one when we
can have a little of both?

16
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:54,980
A creme brulee?

17
00:01:02,360 --> 00:01:03,500
Or something else!

18
00:01:03,680 --> 00:01:06,217
Whatever it takes to cheer
you up and make you smile!

19
00:01:06,300 --> 00:01:08,241
I am perfectly cheery, thank you.

20
00:01:08,380 --> 00:01:09,760
Oh, well, okay.

21
00:01:10,060 --> 00:01:12,180
Then how about a big hug? A hug?

22
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:13,400
Absolutely not.

23
00:01:14,440 --> 00:01:15,917
Mmm, alright thinking.

24
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:17,940
You're beautiful and I love you!

25
00:01:19,240 --> 00:01:21,837
Yes, and for the thousandth
time, I hate you.

26
00:01:21,920 --> 00:01:25,140
Honestly, you're as incorrigible
as ever, aren't you?

27
00:01:26,160 --> 00:01:28,748
Now stop chit-chatting
and get back to work.

28
00:01:29,280 --> 00:01:30,110
Yes, ma 'am!

29
00:01:30,320 --> 00:01:33,555
Oh, and before I forget, a
letter came for you earlier.

30
00:01:34,100 --> 00:01:35,560
A letter from whom?

31
00:01:40,800 --> 00:01:42,980
It's from a Miss Manaria Seuss.

32
00:01:43,980 --> 00:01:45,340
Sister wrote to me?

33
00:01:47,740 --> 00:01:52,200
My dearest Claire, I hope this
letter finds you in good health.

34
00:01:53,060 --> 00:01:57,357
I apologize for the short notice,
and any surprise this may bring.

35
00:01:57,440 --> 00:02:00,077
Know that my heart, unwavering.

36
00:02:00,160 --> 00:02:01,977
Remains by your side.

37
00:02:02,060 --> 00:02:04,160
With all my love.

38
00:02:07,780 --> 00:02:09,660
I know what that means.

39
00:02:10,460 --> 00:02:11,560
She's coming?

40
00:02:24,460 --> 00:02:27,777
Do you want me to

41
00:02:27,860 --> 00:02:34,860
hold

42
00:02:40,560 --> 00:02:41,390
on?

43
00:02:48,600 --> 00:02:50,000
Oh

44
00:03:38,900 --> 00:03:40,560
I love you?

45
00:04:11,900 --> 00:04:14,417
Only the battle for succession has been a

46
00:04:14,500 --> 00:04:17,177
fearsome one and I was
driven off as a casualty.

47
00:04:17,260 --> 00:04:22,337
It's not a pretty story but I
am no longer true royalty so

48
00:04:22,420 --> 00:04:25,717
please I ask that you treat me
as an equal and nothing more.

49
00:04:25,800 --> 00:04:31,517
It's been so

50
00:04:31,600 --> 00:04:33,197
long far too long.

51
00:04:33,280 --> 00:04:37,477
If you ask me I'm happy to see
you looking well well enough.

52
00:04:37,560 --> 00:04:42,520
Goodness you're You're even more
beautiful than I remember. Oh, stop.

53
00:04:42,820 --> 00:04:44,320
You're such a flatterer.

54
00:04:46,500 --> 00:04:47,760
And who is this?

55
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:50,353
Oh, just one of the members of my staff.

56
00:04:50,540 --> 00:04:52,011
Well, introduce yourself.

57
00:04:52,700 --> 00:04:54,288
Greetings, I am Ray Taylor.

58
00:04:54,600 --> 00:04:56,247
It's a pleasure to meet you.

59
00:04:56,460 --> 00:04:59,872
I tend to miss Claire's needs,
both domestic and romantic.

60
00:05:00,440 --> 00:05:01,270
Pardon?

61
00:05:01,400 --> 00:05:02,440
Enough, commoner.

62
00:05:02,620 --> 00:05:05,177
Stop playing games and tell
her what your job really is.

63
00:05:05,260 --> 00:05:06,090
Miss Claire!

64
00:05:06,200 --> 00:05:08,217
I can't just tell people
I'm your love slave.

65
00:05:08,300 --> 00:05:09,377
Think of the scandal!

66
00:05:09,460 --> 00:05:10,717
That is not what you are!

67
00:05:10,800 --> 00:05:13,277
Use the correct term
or get out of my sight!

68
00:05:13,360 --> 00:05:16,536
But if I'm not your love
slave, then what am I to you?

69
00:05:16,640 --> 00:05:17,497
Servant or maid?

70
00:05:17,580 --> 00:05:18,462
Take your pick!

71
00:05:22,120 --> 00:05:22,950
Forgive me.

72
00:05:23,140 --> 00:05:24,160
It's Ray, right?

73
00:05:24,360 --> 00:05:25,536
You're really funny.

74
00:05:27,020 --> 00:05:27,850
Interesting.

75
00:05:28,660 --> 00:05:31,542
You're more than an ordinary
servant, aren't you?

76
00:05:34,340 --> 00:05:36,697
How dare they discard
someone of your caliber?

77
00:05:36,780 --> 00:05:38,737
And favor such a dullard for the throne!

78
00:05:38,820 --> 00:05:41,757
King Seuss must not
appreciate true excellence.

79
00:05:41,840 --> 00:05:43,557
It's not like that!

80
00:05:43,640 --> 00:05:46,297
I mean, my mother isn't his legal wife.

81
00:05:46,380 --> 00:05:47,917
Well, no, but...

82
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:51,737
If anything, I find solace in
being away from all the turmoil.

83
00:05:51,820 --> 00:05:53,760
Family discord is never fun.

84
00:05:54,680 --> 00:05:55,757
Enough on that.

85
00:05:55,840 --> 00:05:57,597
I want to know more about you, Ray?

86
00:05:57,680 --> 00:06:00,960
A commoner admitted to the Royal Academy?

87
00:06:01,300 --> 00:06:02,829
You must be very talented.

88
00:06:03,180 --> 00:06:04,220
Not at all.

89
00:06:04,420 --> 00:06:06,697
She doesn't even come close to your level.

90
00:06:06,780 --> 00:06:08,297
Did you think you were special?

91
00:06:08,380 --> 00:06:12,117
That being a dual caster somehow
made you superior to everyone else?

92
00:06:12,200 --> 00:06:15,540
Well, my dear sister here
boasts four attributes.

93
00:06:15,900 --> 00:06:17,900
She's the world's only quadcaster.

94
00:06:18,180 --> 00:06:20,360
Look at that adorable smug face.

95
00:06:20,580 --> 00:06:22,817
She sounds like she's
bragging about her daughter.

96
00:06:22,900 --> 00:06:24,517
Are you even listening to me?

97
00:06:24,600 --> 00:06:25,718
I love you so much.

98
00:06:25,860 --> 00:06:27,154
Obviously you are not.

99
00:06:28,800 --> 00:06:31,677
Talent for magic is
something you're born with.

100
00:06:31,760 --> 00:06:34,617
It's not as though I did
anything to earn this power.

101
00:06:34,700 --> 00:06:36,357
Why boast about it?

102
00:06:36,440 --> 00:06:41,160
How can you say that your power is
a sign that god has blessed you?

103
00:06:42,280 --> 00:06:44,217
Always exaggerating. I am not.

104
00:06:44,300 --> 00:06:46,717
I felt that blessing for myself.

105
00:06:46,800 --> 00:06:48,697
Meeting you was a gift.

106
00:06:48,780 --> 00:06:51,377
When I wouldn't trade for
anything in the world.

107
00:06:51,460 --> 00:06:55,977
When I lost my mother,
I couldn't even cry.

108
00:06:56,060 --> 00:07:00,100
I was paralyzed with
guilt and self-loathing.

109
00:07:00,500 --> 00:07:03,853
This part of her past isn't
something the game goes into.

110
00:07:04,120 --> 00:07:06,708
It's just a backdrop
to the initial setting.

111
00:07:07,280 --> 00:07:09,780
Duke Francois had business to attend to.

112
00:07:10,940 --> 00:07:12,520
So after his wife's death,

113
00:07:12,760 --> 00:07:17,113
he left young Miss Claire at the home
of a distant relative, Count Larnak.

114
00:07:18,720 --> 00:07:21,580
Which is where she met Princess Manaria.

115
00:07:29,360 --> 00:07:31,317
Pleasure to meet you, my lady.

116
00:07:31,400 --> 00:07:34,020
Why does such a pretty girl look so sad?

117
00:07:43,760 --> 00:07:45,037
My mother...

118
00:07:45,120 --> 00:07:47,277
I said something awful to her.

119
00:07:47,360 --> 00:07:51,840
And I don't think I can
ever forgive myself for it.

120
00:07:58,200 --> 00:08:00,317
Listen, nobody blames you, Claire.

121
00:08:00,400 --> 00:08:01,600
I promise.

122
00:08:15,160 --> 00:08:17,480
Those words became my salvation.

123
00:08:17,760 --> 00:08:19,420
A lifeline in my mind.

124
00:08:20,960 --> 00:08:22,380
How time flies.

125
00:08:22,720 --> 00:08:24,937
Can you believe it's been
ten years since then?

126
00:08:25,020 --> 00:08:25,850
It has.

127
00:08:26,320 --> 00:08:29,614
But I still remember every
moment like it was yesterday.

128
00:08:40,680 --> 00:08:44,900
I swear to you here and now that
I will always be your protector.

129
00:08:53,860 --> 00:08:57,240
In that moment, it was
like you were glowing.

130
00:08:59,980 --> 00:09:02,060
Una, you'll never believe this!

131
00:09:02,180 --> 00:09:05,239
I met the most wonderful,
handsome, charming prince!

132
00:09:07,880 --> 00:09:10,780
Oh yes, I forgot about that.

133
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:13,057
You thought I was a boy
back when we first met.

134
00:09:13,140 --> 00:09:14,320
Yes, well,

135
00:09:14,520 --> 00:09:16,257
you were as charming as any prince,

136
00:09:16,340 --> 00:09:19,928
so you can hardly blame me for
thinking that's what you were.

137
00:09:21,220 --> 00:09:24,780
I was shocked when I found
out the truth. Oh, were you?

138
00:09:30,820 --> 00:09:32,526
Did you hear about that girl?

139
00:09:32,920 --> 00:09:34,744
Apparently, her name's Manaria.

140
00:09:34,940 --> 00:09:37,705
Yeah, and she's a princess
of the Zeus kingdom.

141
00:09:38,360 --> 00:09:39,560
Wow! Are you right?

142
00:09:41,080 --> 00:09:42,720
Oh my, are you alright?

143
00:09:43,300 --> 00:09:44,660
This is so fun.

144
00:09:44,840 --> 00:09:45,857
Yeah, I mean, I'm fine.

145
00:09:45,940 --> 00:09:46,770
Thank you for your help.

146
00:09:46,853 --> 00:09:47,683
Good.

147
00:09:47,766 --> 00:09:48,596
I'm glad to hear it.

148
00:09:48,679 --> 00:09:49,675
That was a close one.

149
00:09:49,960 --> 00:09:51,280
Be safe, my dear.

150
00:09:54,760 --> 00:09:55,590
Oh, no.

151
00:09:55,720 --> 00:09:56,757
I've kept you waiting.

152
00:09:56,840 --> 00:09:58,440
I'm sorry. Oh, don't be.

153
00:09:58,680 --> 00:10:00,268
I wasn't waiting that long.

154
00:10:20,440 --> 00:10:22,381
As the Amour Ceremony approaches,

155
00:10:22,560 --> 00:10:25,737
today's class will delve into
Poesy, Amour, and other poems.

156
00:10:25,820 --> 00:10:30,114
Let the Verses of Love guide us through
this enchanting literary journey.

157
00:10:31,200 --> 00:10:32,900
Ray, have you got a moment?

158
00:10:33,640 --> 00:10:35,797
I hope I'm not catching you off guard,

159
00:10:35,880 --> 00:10:38,737
but I wanted to chat, and
magic makes it so easy.

160
00:10:38,820 --> 00:10:40,100
Oh, but don't worry.

161
00:10:40,380 --> 00:10:43,057
I can't go poking around
in your private thoughts.

162
00:10:43,140 --> 00:10:44,180
I'm aware.

163
00:10:44,500 --> 00:10:47,971
You're using telepathic speech,
which is wind magic, right?

164
00:10:48,400 --> 00:10:50,937
Ah, I should have known
you'd be on top of it.

165
00:10:51,020 --> 00:10:52,057
You know how to connect?

166
00:10:52,140 --> 00:10:55,357
You already did the hardest part for
me by establishing the magic channel.

167
00:10:55,440 --> 00:10:57,616
It was actually a breeze to tap into.

168
00:10:58,080 --> 00:11:00,780
So, uh, what's going on? Oh, nothing.

169
00:11:01,100 --> 00:11:03,276
I just wanted to know more about you.

170
00:11:03,620 --> 00:11:04,450
Here we go.

171
00:11:04,820 --> 00:11:08,337
Princess Manaria appears in the
game as an ally to the player.

172
00:11:08,420 --> 00:11:11,117
Miss Claire always wants to spend
time with her when she's around,

173
00:11:11,200 --> 00:11:12,480
which distracts Ms.

174
00:11:12,600 --> 00:11:15,577
Claire and gives the player
more time with the princes.

175
00:11:15,660 --> 00:11:17,737
Manaria comes in around
the middle of the game,

176
00:11:17,820 --> 00:11:20,137
and she can be super
helpful for your strategy.

177
00:11:20,220 --> 00:11:23,277
Because she's so useful,
she's a favor for most fans.

178
00:11:23,360 --> 00:11:25,889
But she's a total
freaking buzzkill for me!

179
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:30,097
I couldn't care less about the princes,
and much prefer to rendezvous with Ms.

180
00:11:30,180 --> 00:11:31,010
Claire.

181
00:11:31,093 --> 00:11:34,517
So in my mind, Princess Manaria
transforms from an ally to a rival.

182
00:11:34,600 --> 00:11:37,517
It's not that I'm not a fan of hers,
but the fact that she steals Ms.

183
00:11:37,600 --> 00:11:38,430
Claire away sucks!

184
00:11:38,513 --> 00:11:41,080
And now that makes her my enemy.

185
00:11:41,720 --> 00:11:42,550
Ray?

186
00:11:43,120 --> 00:11:43,950
Hello?

187
00:11:44,660 --> 00:11:46,660
I'm sorry, can you still hear me?

188
00:11:46,820 --> 00:11:48,340
Yes, irritatingly well.

189
00:11:48,640 --> 00:11:50,540
I mean, of course I can!

190
00:11:50,780 --> 00:11:51,898
Almost too clearly.

191
00:11:52,300 --> 00:11:54,137
Anyway, there's not much to tell.

192
00:11:54,220 --> 00:11:55,957
I'm just your average commoner.

193
00:11:56,040 --> 00:11:59,537
I'm pretty sure there's nothing about
me that would remotely interest you.

194
00:11:59,620 --> 00:12:01,032
Now if you'll excuse me.

195
00:12:03,440 --> 00:12:06,457
Well, that's a reaction I've
never experienced before.

196
00:12:06,540 --> 00:12:08,187
Now I'm even more intrigued.

197
00:12:09,520 --> 00:12:10,760
I'm so impressed.

198
00:12:11,060 --> 00:12:14,557
Your reading of that poem today
was amazing, Princess Manaria.

199
00:12:14,640 --> 00:12:15,470
Question though,

200
00:12:15,553 --> 00:12:17,757
why the shift from the
usual I dedicate this

201
00:12:17,840 --> 00:12:20,177
poem to you to I deliver this poem to you?

202
00:12:20,260 --> 00:12:21,337
I mean, it's cool either way.

203
00:12:21,420 --> 00:12:22,457
I was just wondering.

204
00:12:22,540 --> 00:12:23,370
Ah, yes.

205
00:12:23,453 --> 00:12:26,477
An old form of prosody I
borrowed from an ancient poem.

206
00:12:26,560 --> 00:12:27,795
You're well, Red Ray.

207
00:12:27,940 --> 00:12:31,120
Would you care to join
the discussion? Oh, um,

208
00:12:31,380 --> 00:12:33,377
I'm not exactly a big poetry gal,

209
00:12:33,460 --> 00:12:35,997
so I'm afraid I'm going to
have to pass on that offer.

210
00:12:36,080 --> 00:12:37,417
Sorry, I hope that's okay.

211
00:12:37,500 --> 00:12:38,330
Seriously?

212
00:12:38,540 --> 00:12:41,297
How can you say no to an
invite from Princess Manaria?

213
00:12:41,380 --> 00:12:44,615
Having talent doesn't mean
you can afford to get cocky.

214
00:12:45,100 --> 00:12:45,930
Wow.

215
00:12:46,013 --> 00:12:47,440
Is Rey truly that brilliant?

216
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:48,840
That she is.

217
00:12:49,120 --> 00:12:51,337
She can take on anyone in a magic battle.

218
00:12:51,420 --> 00:12:53,180
Oh, hey, Prince Rod. Really?

219
00:12:53,520 --> 00:12:55,117
Well, that sounds intriguing.

220
00:12:55,200 --> 00:12:57,141
I'd like to have a bout with her.

221
00:12:57,280 --> 00:12:58,700
Yeah, well, get ready.

222
00:12:58,860 --> 00:13:01,577
Because you can't face her like
you would a normal opponent.

223
00:13:01,660 --> 00:13:05,297
I played chess against her one
time, and she left my head spinning.

224
00:13:05,380 --> 00:13:07,157
She eluded even you, Prince Rod?

225
00:13:07,240 --> 00:13:08,070
Oh, yeah.

226
00:13:08,540 --> 00:13:09,481
How fascinating.

227
00:13:09,920 --> 00:13:14,155
But hey, if you're looking for a bout,
I'd be happy to oblige, shall we?

228
00:13:14,240 --> 00:13:15,070
You know,

229
00:13:15,153 --> 00:13:16,577
I was hoping I'd get
the chance to see your

230
00:13:16,660 --> 00:13:18,817
minions in action while
I was here in Bower.

231
00:13:18,900 --> 00:13:19,730
Is that a yes?

232
00:13:19,813 --> 00:13:21,717
I hope you know what you're getting into.

233
00:13:21,800 --> 00:13:23,565
Sounds like a good time to me.

234
00:13:33,180 --> 00:13:34,380
You ready for this?

235
00:13:34,560 --> 00:13:36,477
Hope you don't mind if I go all out.

236
00:13:36,560 --> 00:13:38,380
Please be my guest.

237
00:13:38,900 --> 00:13:42,797
You know, you've got a lot of people
talking about your skills as a quadcaster.

238
00:13:42,880 --> 00:13:44,998
Let's see what all the fuck's about!

239
00:13:49,200 --> 00:13:50,847
Wow, would you look at that!

240
00:14:03,620 --> 00:14:05,137
That was excellently done!

241
00:14:05,220 --> 00:14:08,600
She's fast, and her precision
is exceptional, too.

242
00:14:09,020 --> 00:14:10,440
You didn't even flinch?

243
00:14:10,600 --> 00:14:12,680
How about this thing? Attack!

244
00:14:17,040 --> 00:14:18,100
And burst!

245
00:14:22,860 --> 00:14:24,300
Oh, no, sister!

246
00:14:29,020 --> 00:14:31,780
You have some firepower, Prince Rod.

247
00:14:32,100 --> 00:14:34,577
The rumors sell you short. I'm impressed.

248
00:14:34,660 --> 00:14:36,160
That was amazing!

249
00:14:36,480 --> 00:14:38,360
Earth magic this time, is it?

250
00:14:38,800 --> 00:14:41,060
Let's see, what should I do now?

251
00:14:41,360 --> 00:14:44,889
It seems rather uncouth to fight
fire with fire, so maybe...

252
00:14:45,240 --> 00:14:47,240
Something a little more like this?

253
00:14:55,480 --> 00:14:56,420
Ice minions?

254
00:14:57,440 --> 00:15:00,558
Oh, pretty bold of you to
use my own move against me.

255
00:15:00,660 --> 00:15:02,117
Are you prepared to surrender?

256
00:15:02,200 --> 00:15:03,540
Oh, definitely not.

257
00:15:03,720 --> 00:15:05,677
And I don't think you want me to either.

258
00:15:05,760 --> 00:15:07,380
So, let's do this!

259
00:15:07,660 --> 00:15:10,900
I'll be curious to see just
how long you can keep up!

260
00:15:32,460 --> 00:15:35,754
If he draws this out, she'll
be at a major disadvantage.

261
00:15:36,160 --> 00:15:38,360
That would be true for anyone else.

262
00:15:39,620 --> 00:15:41,380
Watch closely and you'll see.

263
00:15:41,900 --> 00:15:44,782
Princess Manaria has an
ace or two up her sleeve.

264
00:15:47,700 --> 00:15:50,700
All right, got it. Let's go!

265
00:15:50,980 --> 00:15:52,757
Do you think she can still win?

266
00:15:52,840 --> 00:15:55,617
Well, they've both got
plenty of fight left in them.

267
00:15:55,700 --> 00:15:56,717
Only time will tell.

268
00:15:56,800 --> 00:15:58,918
But she can't keep this up for long!

269
00:15:59,180 --> 00:16:03,062
Rod is using his immense amount
of magical power to wear her down!

270
00:16:03,460 --> 00:16:06,500
He's going to overwhelm
her just like he did Misha!

271
00:16:18,180 --> 00:16:19,180
Where'd they go?

272
00:16:27,880 --> 00:16:29,780
Fine. I surrender.

273
00:16:30,300 --> 00:16:31,620
That was amazing!

274
00:16:34,820 --> 00:16:37,260
That was a brilliant showing.

275
00:16:37,440 --> 00:16:39,240
Professor Torrid. Class.

276
00:16:39,480 --> 00:16:41,337
The last spell that was used?

277
00:16:41,420 --> 00:16:42,600
Who can name it?

278
00:16:43,340 --> 00:16:45,180
It's called Spellbreaker.

279
00:16:46,520 --> 00:16:48,040
That is correct.

280
00:16:48,660 --> 00:16:53,880
It analyzes a spell's composition, forces
itself into it, and undoes it completely.

281
00:16:54,240 --> 00:16:56,220
It's magic that erases magic.

282
00:16:57,120 --> 00:17:00,617
She can evaluate and tear apart
a spell in the middle of combat?

283
00:17:00,700 --> 00:17:02,582
I had no idea that was possible.

284
00:17:02,960 --> 00:17:04,842
For most people, it wouldn't be.

285
00:17:04,980 --> 00:17:08,640
When it comes to water, earth,
and fire, her aptitude is high.

286
00:17:08,800 --> 00:17:11,976
But in wind, she's even
stronger, ranking exceptional.

287
00:17:14,540 --> 00:17:15,420
All true.

288
00:17:15,760 --> 00:17:17,936
There's more to it than that, though.

289
00:17:18,100 --> 00:17:20,982
Something that makes her
magic truly frightening.

290
00:17:22,680 --> 00:17:24,151
Forgive my crude methods.

291
00:17:24,340 --> 00:17:27,117
You're a very difficult girl
to figure out, you know that?

292
00:17:27,200 --> 00:17:28,788
I get that a lot, actually.

293
00:17:38,140 --> 00:17:39,720
Sister was incredible!

294
00:17:40,620 --> 00:17:44,717
Yes, Spellbreaker was fantastic, but do
you know what I found more impressive?

295
00:17:44,800 --> 00:17:45,630
What's that?

296
00:17:45,713 --> 00:17:49,340
The way she faced Prince Rod so
boldly with no hesitation. Yeah.

297
00:17:49,800 --> 00:17:53,217
It was like watching a battle between
the mythical gods of beauty and war.

298
00:17:53,300 --> 00:17:54,520
Sure, if you say so.

299
00:17:55,320 --> 00:17:56,150
Sure?

300
00:17:56,233 --> 00:17:57,637
That's quite the tepid response.

301
00:17:57,720 --> 00:18:00,700
Are you in a foul mood
for some reason? Who, me?

302
00:18:00,940 --> 00:18:02,040
No, just Peachy.

303
00:18:04,560 --> 00:18:05,800
Hold on a moment.

304
00:18:06,120 --> 00:18:07,517
Could it be you're jealous?

305
00:18:07,600 --> 00:18:08,800
Yes! That was fast!

306
00:18:09,400 --> 00:18:11,517
There isn't much sense in denying it,

307
00:18:11,600 --> 00:18:13,857
considering how clear I've
made my feelings for you.

308
00:18:13,940 --> 00:18:16,857
Just because you've made them clear
doesn't mean that I accept them.

309
00:18:16,940 --> 00:18:19,757
What can I do to make you
realize that I'm serious?

310
00:18:19,840 --> 00:18:21,940
Nothing, so let's leave it at that.

311
00:18:22,840 --> 00:18:24,217
Though, I suppose...

312
00:18:24,300 --> 00:18:29,060
If you would show your devotion, place
an offering upon the scales for me.

313
00:18:29,340 --> 00:18:33,420
Above all, the flowers of flora
will prove your love's veracity.

314
00:18:34,640 --> 00:18:37,060
That's from Poesia More. Indeed.

315
00:18:37,980 --> 00:18:42,120
Poesia More is a poetic retelling
of an old Bauer Kingdom legend.

316
00:18:43,940 --> 00:18:48,217
The story goes that there were two suitors
who fell in love with the same priestess.

317
00:18:48,300 --> 00:18:52,947
Both were powerful men, so the conflict
between them echoed through the nation,

318
00:18:53,140 --> 00:18:54,493
plunging it into chaos.

319
00:18:55,120 --> 00:18:57,237
Troubled to be the source of such strife,

320
00:18:57,320 --> 00:18:59,377
the priestess prayed and God presented her

321
00:18:59,460 --> 00:19:02,160
with a set of scales
along with these words.

322
00:19:02,340 --> 00:19:06,317
Let those who would wed you place
their offerings upon these scales.

323
00:19:06,400 --> 00:19:09,897
They will tip in favor of the
man who is to be your husband.

324
00:19:09,980 --> 00:19:12,237
In accordance with the scale's judgment,

325
00:19:12,320 --> 00:19:15,791
the priestess married the man
who offered flowers of flora.

326
00:19:16,120 --> 00:19:20,760
As for the man who lost in love, he
went on to become an excellent king.

327
00:19:22,440 --> 00:19:25,560
From that ancient legend
came the Amur ceremony,

328
00:19:25,800 --> 00:19:27,976
which is still performed to this day.

329
00:19:28,440 --> 00:19:29,270
Hold on.

330
00:19:29,440 --> 00:19:33,558
You mean, the scales of love mentioned
in Poesia Amur really do exist?

331
00:19:33,680 --> 00:19:36,268
They're most likely
some kind of magic tool.

332
00:19:36,420 --> 00:19:39,657
Items with magic stones in
them have been around for ages.

333
00:19:39,740 --> 00:19:43,237
People have used them since long
before we knew how they worked.

334
00:19:43,320 --> 00:19:45,197
Suitors' offerings are still placed upon

335
00:19:45,280 --> 00:19:47,497
the scales of love
during the Amor ceremony.

336
00:19:47,580 --> 00:19:51,097
Even now, people use it to choose
who they're going to marry.

337
00:19:51,180 --> 00:19:54,317
Sort of like a cross between an
arranged marriage and a duel.

338
00:19:54,400 --> 00:19:57,160
Or a high-stakes
reenactment of Poesia Amor.

339
00:19:57,420 --> 00:19:58,837
Famed artifact or not,

340
00:19:58,920 --> 00:20:03,557
very few people are truly willing to entrust
their futures to such a farcical game.

341
00:20:03,640 --> 00:20:05,237
And there are those
who use the ceremony as

342
00:20:05,320 --> 00:20:07,457
an excuse to confess
their love every time.

343
00:20:07,540 --> 00:20:11,197
People are always waiting to see
who will confess and to whom what?

344
00:20:11,280 --> 00:20:14,037
A fascinating tradition and so romantic!

345
00:20:14,120 --> 00:20:17,040
I see now why everyone
is so giddy about it!

346
00:20:17,680 --> 00:20:18,510
So?

347
00:20:19,520 --> 00:20:23,720
Who among us will be putting their
love to the test on the scales?

348
00:20:26,360 --> 00:20:27,997
You can sit this one out, Claire?

349
00:20:28,080 --> 00:20:30,840
You've already got Ray Prince, you.

350
00:20:31,580 --> 00:20:35,157
Another mystery solved, so that's
how it is between the two of you?

351
00:20:35,240 --> 00:20:37,897
Then the last thing I need
is someone else spouting this

352
00:20:37,980 --> 00:20:41,257
nonsense and that's what it
is—the girl is only teasing me,

353
00:20:41,340 --> 00:20:42,170
nothing more.

354
00:20:42,253 --> 00:20:45,657
You still really believe I'm not being
sincere about my feelings for you?

355
00:20:45,740 --> 00:20:47,997
So it's unrequited love on Ray's part?

356
00:20:48,080 --> 00:20:51,797
Hmm—love given but not
returned or acknowledged.

357
00:20:51,880 --> 00:20:52,977
Well, well.

358
00:20:53,060 --> 00:20:54,160
And anyway,

359
00:20:54,900 --> 00:20:57,177
if I were to court a
partner of the same gender,

360
00:20:57,260 --> 00:20:59,477
I would obviously choose sister over you.

361
00:20:59,560 --> 00:21:01,197
Must be hard to hear, huh?

362
00:21:01,280 --> 00:21:04,977
As much as you may adore her,
Claire says that she prefers me.

363
00:21:05,060 --> 00:21:06,001
Goodness—this is

364
00:21:09,440 --> 00:21:11,377
a rather sudden display of affection.

365
00:21:11,460 --> 00:21:15,437
Tell me, if I said that I loved
you, would you believe me, Claire?

366
00:21:15,520 --> 00:21:16,917
Of course I would.

367
00:21:17,000 --> 00:21:20,457
In all these years, I've never
doubted the sincerity of your love.

368
00:21:20,540 --> 00:21:22,397
Don't let your head explode, Ray.

369
00:21:22,480 --> 00:21:23,837
Cute numbers or something?

370
00:21:23,920 --> 00:21:25,449
Sister, stop—I'm blushing.

371
00:21:28,740 --> 00:21:30,540
2, 3, 5, 7,

372
00:21:32,220 --> 00:21:34,940
11, 13, 17, 19, 23, 29, 31, 37, 31?

373
00:21:35,040 --> 00:21:37,017
Those two get along well?

374
00:21:37,100 --> 00:21:38,597
They must be quite close?

375
00:21:38,680 --> 00:21:40,597
must be quite close More tea, anyone?

376
00:21:40,680 --> 00:21:42,677
All this chatting must be thirsty work.

377
00:21:42,760 --> 00:21:45,320
Thank you, but that isn't the teapot.

378
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:47,277
It's the milk pitcher.

379
00:21:47,360 --> 00:21:49,420
Right, terribly sorry about that.

380
00:21:49,940 --> 00:21:51,280
You look rather pale.

381
00:21:51,820 --> 00:21:53,140
Have you fallen ill?

382
00:21:53,280 --> 00:21:56,760
Oh no, I'm perfectly fine I
appreciate the concern, though.

383
00:21:59,280 --> 00:22:00,640
What about when's name?

384
00:22:00,800 --> 00:22:02,577
He's the one you're
supposed to be in love with,

385
00:22:02,660 --> 00:22:04,960
not that quad-testing royal interloper.

386
00:22:06,380 --> 00:22:07,717
Should I have said when?

387
00:22:07,800 --> 00:22:08,780
Wow ...

388
00:22:44,440 --> 00:22:45,840
Oh

389
00:23:11,080 --> 00:23:16,000
I don't know.

390
00:23:36,800 --> 00:23:37,800
I'm going to die.

391
00:23:38,800 --> 00:23:41,337
I'm not going to die.

392
00:23:41,420 --> 00:23:42,660
I'm going to die.
